## Why GPL-3.0

Recorded as ADR 0001. In short: this project draws design inspiration from
`yzyray/lizzieyzy` and its fork `wimi321/lizzieyzy-next`, which are GPL-3.0.
The moment any file, asset, or reverse-engineered protocol is *derived* from
that lineage rather than independently reimplemented, GPL-3.0 becomes
mandatory. Choosing MIT first and discovering a derivation later would require
every contributor's consent to relicense.

GPL-3.0 also absorbs MIT-licensed code one-way, so inspiration from
`wimi321/GoAgent` (MIT) carries no friction.

